Hugging Face, in collaboration with @therobotstudio , @WowRobo, @seeedstudio , and Partabot, has launched SO-101 — an affordable, open-source robot arm designed specifically for AI developers. Priced between $100 and $500 depending on assembly level and shipping, the SO-101 builds on the success of the earlier SO-100 and is aimed at making robotics more accessible to a broader community. Fully integrated with Hugging Face’s robotics ecosystem, including @LeRobotHF and @pollenrobotics , the arm allows users to easily modify and improve both hardware and software.
@ClementDelangue , @huggingface’s co-founder and CEO, called the SO-101 “the first robot arms any AI builder should buy,” encouraging developers to experiment and innovate using the new model. Full documentation and setup guides are available on Hugging Face’s GitHub. As part of its continued commitment to open-source innovation, Hugging Face hopes the SO-101 will empower a new wave of creativity in AI robotics, inviting community members to contribute and share their projects.
